---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Tagline from '../components/Tagline.astro';
---

<Base title="About — yakar.me" description="Ahmet Yakar: software engineer, writer and traveller.">
  <article class="flex flex-col gap-14 px-6 pt-9 pb-24 desk:px-24 desk:pt-26">
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-7 border-b border-line pb-8">
      <Tagline />
      <h1 class="font-display text-d2 desk:text-d1">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose max-w-170">
      <p>
        I’m Ahmet. I studied mechatronics engineering, but somewhere between the motors and the control loops I realised the
        part I liked most was the code. Nine years later I’m a senior backend engineer, building large-scale systems in the
        defence industry — mostly Java, mostly distributed and event-driven.
      </p>
      <p>
        The part of the job I can’t get enough of is concurrency. It’s where software stops being deterministic, and the
        question becomes: how do you use a system you can barely control — and use it perfectly well? It is never boring. I
        write about it <a href="/writing/">here</a>, along with PostgreSQL internals. I was writing long before either, and not
        only about software; writing is simply one of the things that makes me happy.
      </p>
      <p>
        At work, people tend to come to me when they want something explained — not just what it does, but why it was built
        that way, in words that make it click. The conversations rarely stay technical for long. Philosophy, science, books
        and music usually find their way in.
      </p>
      <p>
        I learn on purpose. Most of what I study runs on a plan, and I’ve made peace with being that person. Outside work I
        play the saxophone and take photographs. I can lose an entire evening to a video deriving some physics equation, and I
        think black holes are the most interesting objects in the universe. I’m happiest in nature and a little less so in
        crowds. I love learning languages and travelling — so far a good part of Asia and most of Europe. Football, I have to
        admit, remains a complete mystery to me.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lately I’m most interested in payments and financial systems, where correctness is measured in cents. If you’d like to
        talk about backend systems — or anything above — <a href="mailto:ahmet@yakar.me">my inbox is open</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
